### Component 7 — Secure Cache & Encryption Hardening

#### [AUDIT-IN-PLACE] [secureCache.ts](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts)

Verify and harden the following during implementation:

- [ ] **PBKDF2 iterations:** Currently 100,000 — verify this meets OWASP 2024 minimum (600,000 for SHA-256). Consider increasing or migrating to Argon2id
- [ ] **IV reuse:** Each [put()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts#192-238) generates a fresh 12-byte IV via `crypto.getRandomValues()` — ✅ correct
- [ ] **Key derivation scope:** Salt includes `dbName + origin` — verify no two origins share a key
- [ ] **Max entry size:** 5MB limit prevents DoS via oversized entries — ✅
- [ ] **Decryption failure:** On failure, entry is deleted (fail-closed) — ✅
- [ ] **Side-channel:** `Array.from()` on encrypted data creates a copy — verify no timing leaks in comparison ops
- [ ] **Seed storage:** Seed in `localStorage` survives clear-site-data — ensure logout clears it
- [ ] **Schema version mismatch:** Old schema entries are silently ignored — verify no data loss path

