### Attack Vectors — Specific Checks
| # | Vector | Check | Priority |
|---|--------|-------|----------|
| A1 | **WS Denial of Service** | Verify server enforces max message size and rate per connection | High |
| A2 | **Cache timing attack** | Encrypted cache read time shouldn't reveal plaintext length | Medium |
| A3 | **SW update hijack** | Ensure SW served with `Cache-Control: no-cache` to prevent stale SW | High |
| A4 | **IndexedDB quota exhaustion** | `MAX_ENTRY_BYTES` (5MB) caps individual entries, but verify total DB size is bounded | Medium |
| A5 | **Polling amplification** | If admin sets poll to 100ms with 1000 concurrent users, verify server can handle 10k req/s | High |
| A6 | **CORS misconfiguration** | Verify API returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` only for trusted origins | High |
| A7 | **Prototype pollution** | Verify `JSON.parse()` results are not spread onto prototypes | Medium |
| A8 | **ReDoS in input validation** | Verify no regex on user input with catastrophic backtracking | Low |
| A9 | **Clickjacking** | Verify `X-Frame-Options: DENY` or CSP `frame-ancestors 'none'` | Medium |
| A10 | **Open redirect** | Verify all navigation uses hardcoded paths, no user-controlled redirect targets | Medium |

